<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109228" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποστολή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fasting,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.129c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				46.20.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>omission of a letter,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ῑ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Adv.</u>
					187.22
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>removal,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				91.26
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>shrinking, timidity, evasion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ep.Hebr.
				10.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ὑποστολῆς</span>”
				<i>holding back,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ascl.
					<u>Tact.</u>
					10.21
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετά τινος ὑ.</span> with a
			certain <i>reserve,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.108
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>concealment, dissimulation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				2.14.2
			</span></i>.</div>
